{"term":"maximal","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1e60a44518c3a7c0e4","definition":"Largest, greatest (in magnitude), highest, most.","example":"The organification of iodide in the thyroid gland was described using a second order rate constant (KthybindC, /nmol/L*hr/kg thyroid weight) fitted to provide thyroidal iodide stores near the maximal value, which increased with age.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["extreme","maximum","ultimate","extreme","ferocious","exquisite","intense","almighty","greatest","highest","maximal","maximum","passing","raging","ultimate","utmost","uttermost"],"antonyms":["minimal"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bimaximal","halfmaximal","maximal ideal","maximalism","maximalist","maximality","maximalize","maximally","maximal munch","multimaximal","nonmaximal","perimaximal","postmaximal","premaximal","submaximal","supermaximal","supramaximal","tribimaximal","trimaximal","ultramaximal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maximal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f8e65b9b77dd0a40c5","definition":"Larger than any previous term in the sequence.","example":"In the sequence (1, 2, 10, 5, 12, 6), the fifth term, f(5) = 12, is a maximal term, as each of the first 4 terms are smaller than 12.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["minimal"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["bimaximal","halfmaximal","maximal ideal","maximalism","maximalist","maximality","maximalize","maximally","maximal munch","multimaximal","nonmaximal","perimaximal","postmaximal","premaximal","submaximal","supermaximal","supramaximal","tribimaximal","trimaximal","ultramaximal"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maximal#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8f9591b579fd0aa513","definition":"Such that no other element is grea